PREFIX ex: <https://example.org/>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

# The output contract of `examples/hello.fossil`, and therefore of the
# walking-skeleton invariant. This is ShEx, not fossil: a shape document is a
# separate artefact, and fossil reads it rather than restating it.
#
# One shape is declared here, and its name does three jobs in the program next
# door: `type { Person } := io.shex("hello.shex")` binds it by the LOCAL NAME of
# `ex:Person`, the mapping header names that binding, and the vertex type written
# to disk is that same `Person`.
#
# `ex:Person` declares exactly one predicate, so the body writes exactly one
# property and its bare key is `name` — the last segment of
# `https://example.org/name`. Cardinality is 1..1: the mapping must write it, and
# `check_required_properties` says so if it stops.
#
# Verified against the built binary: `fossil check examples/hello.fossil` exits 0
# and `fossil run` writes 5 `Person` vertices with a `name` column of `string`,
# `rdf_uri = https://example.org/name`, `xsd_datatype = xsd:string`.

ex:Person {
  ex:name xsd:string
}
